Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. The
table below counts the reports the desk merged here by 4 October.

**Merged as one issue, but it is two.** The parser reads dates month first, and our tenants
write the day first: that is `parser`, and its fix is queued. The `booking-v3` form prints
`MM/DD/YYYY` and reads the date day first: that is `hint`, and the parser fix does not close it.

<Callout kind="warn">
Split. Each cause now has its own ticket:
<a href="https://github.com/sbdiarra/megadev-challenges/issues/1">parser</a> and
<a href="https://github.com/sbdiarra/megadev-challenges/issues/4">hint</a>.
The counts and the reasoning are on <a href="/kb/incidents/4471/split">the split page</a>.
</Callout>

